---
name: discover
description: Structural {{LANG_NAME}} codebase navigation using ast-grep. Resolves {{IMPORT_VERB}}s, inspects files, finds definitions, traces reachability, and locates usages via AST. Prefer over grep for reachability questions (is this file live?) and definition lookups (where is this symbol defined?).
---

## Why this exists

{{MOTIVATION}}

**Use `discover.sh` before acting on any grep hit.** If you grep for a symbol and find it, you still don't know if the file is live or if that's even the right definition. `discover.sh` answers those questions.

## Script location

```
{{SCRIPT_PATH}}
```

Run from the repo root. All file paths are relative to repo root.

## Subcommands

### resolve

Resolve a {{LANG_NAME}} {{IMPORT_VERB}} to a repo-relative file path.

```bash
bash {{SCRIPT_PATH}} resolve "{{RESOLVE_EXAMPLE_1}}"
# → {{RESOLVE_RESULT_1}}

bash {{SCRIPT_PATH}} resolve "{{RESOLVE_EXAMPLE_2}}" --from {{RESOLVE_FROM_2}}
# → {{RESOLVE_RESULT_2}}
```

### inspect

Extract structured JSON from a {{LANG_NAME}} file. Filter with {{INSPECT_FLAGS}}. Default is all.

`--depth` controls entity detail: `names` (default), `signatures` (first line), `full` (entire body).

```bash
bash {{SCRIPT_PATH}} inspect {{EXAMPLE_FILE}} --{{IMPORT_SECTION}}
bash {{SCRIPT_PATH}} inspect {{EXAMPLE_FILE}} --entities --depth signatures
bash {{SCRIPT_PATH}} inspect {{EXAMPLE_FILE}} --entities --depth full
```

### definition

Find the exact file and line where a symbol used in a file is defined. Follows the file's {{IMPORT_VERB}} chain. Never guesses.

```bash
bash {{SCRIPT_PATH}} definition {{EXAMPLE_FILE}} {{EXAMPLE_SYMBOL}}
# → {"symbol":"{{EXAMPLE_SYMBOL}}","kind":"class","file":"...","line":17,"via":[]}
```

Exits 1 with `"error": "not found in import graph"` for external packages or symbols that don't exist.

### live-files

BFS from the entry point following all {{IMPORT_VERB}}s. Outputs every reachable file, one per line.

```bash
bash {{SCRIPT_PATH}} live-files
```

### is-live

Check whether a single file is reachable from the entry point.

```bash
bash {{SCRIPT_PATH}} is-live {{EXAMPLE_FILE}}
# → LIVE: {{EXAMPLE_FILE}} (exit 0)
```

### importers

Find every file that {{IMPORT_VERB}}s the given file.

```bash
bash {{SCRIPT_PATH}} importers {{EXAMPLE_FILE}}
```

### usages

Find all references to an ast-grep pattern. `--live-only` filters to files reachable from the entry point.

```bash
bash {{SCRIPT_PATH}} usages '{{USAGE_EXAMPLE_1}}' --live-only
bash {{SCRIPT_PATH}} usages '{{USAGE_EXAMPLE_2}}'
```

The pattern is any valid ast-grep {{LANG_NAME}} pattern — metavariables (`$NAME`, `$$$ARGS`) match structurally.

